<section class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">About the notebook</p>
    <h1>A demonstration,<br><em>not a publication.</em></h1>
    <p class="lead">
        Field Notes exists to show how a Fastify route can hand data to a
        Handlebars template and let the template decide how to present it.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
    <div class="dashboard-grid">
        <article class="panel">
            <p class="eyebrow">What is rendered</p>
            <h2>Dynamic values</h2>
            <ul class="panel-list">
                <li><code>{{totalNotes}}</code> style values come from route data.</li>
                <li>Conditionals hide the featured section when no note is featured.</li>
                <li>Loops render the topic chips and note cards.</li>
                <li>A partial keeps the note card markup in one place.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="panel">
            <p class="eyebrow">What is escaped</p>
            <h2>Safe by default</h2>
            <p>
                All note text uses normal Handlebars expressions. If a note
                contained <code>&lt;script&gt;</code>, Handlebars would display
                it as text instead of executing it.
            </p>
            <p>
                The layout is the only place that uses a triple-brace
                expression, because <code>body</code> contains trusted template
                output rather than visitor input.
            </p>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>
